# Module tests

Every module has its own test file.

- Write `src/<module>.test.ts` before `src/<module>.ts`, in the same folder.
- Import the module under test directly, for example `./result.js`.
- Cover the public barrel separately in `src/index.test.ts`.
- Assert explicit inputs and outputs. Pure functions do not need mocks.
- When behavior is part of the JavaScript API, extend `examples/javascript-esm` and `examples/javascript-cjs` in the same iteration.
- Close the iteration by running the tests and updating the docs.

```typescript
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";
import { map, ok } from "./result.js";

describe("map", () => {
  it("applies the function to an ok value", () => {
    expect(map(ok(2), (n) => n + 1)).toEqual(ok(3));
  });
});
```
